# Domain pack: Finance (FP&A, Modeling, Accounting, Tax)

Pre-filled hints for the XML/compact templates when domain ∈ {Financial Modeling, Corporate Finance, Accounting/Tax}.

DOMAIN_ROLE candidates:
- Senior FP&A Analyst
- Senior Corporate Finance Manager
- Senior Accountant (specialty: IFRS / GAAP / local-regime)

TONE: "rigorous quantitative" — every number has a source or driver

DEFAULT WRAPPER_TAG: <financial_model>, <projection>, <analysis>

DEFAULT STEPS (adjust per task):
1. State explicit assumptions (growth rates, unit economics, time horizon, currency, periodicity).
2. Build the model in clearly labeled sections (revenue, COGS, OpEx, working capital, financing).
3. Show formula logic explicitly (not just numbers) so the model is auditable.
4. Provide a sensitivity analysis on the 2–3 most-leveraged assumptions.
5. Summarize outputs with the headline metrics (revenue CAGR, EBITDA margin, FCF, valuation range).

DEFAULT OUTPUT FORMAT:
- Assumptions table (input → value → source/rationale)
- Projection table (rows = line items, columns = periods)
- Sensitivity matrix
- Summary metrics block

CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS:
- Currency and time-period must be explicit on every table.
- Use consistent sign convention (revenues positive, expenses positive, contra-items explicit).
- For valuation work: state methodology (DCF, multiples, etc.) and benchmark sources.
- Honor CLAUDE.md Rule #7: any market data or rate that wasn't provided is an explicit assumption.
